# PROGRESS.md is an append-only diary, and two laptops add lines to the end of it on the same day.
# Every time that happened (18, 19, 20 and 21 Nov 2026) git stopped with a conflict, the auto-push
# failed, and updates silently stayed off GitHub until somebody noticed - on 18 Nov for a whole day.
# "merge=union" is git's own built-in driver: it simply keeps BOTH sides' lines, which is exactly
# what this file wants. Nothing to install or configure.
PROGRESS.md merge=union

# Same reasoning for the night's bug log: two terminals (builder and tester) both append to it
# on the same night, and a conflict there would stop the auto-push for everything else.
docs/BUGS-TONIGHT.md merge=union

# Never union-merge these: they hold one enormous base64 line each (the modules), so keeping both
# sides would produce two copies of a module and a broken page. They must be resolved properly -
# take one side and re-run the other side's patch script in server/.
index.html      -merge
mail-app.html   -merge
courier_dashboard.html -merge
